{"name":"Hideaway","hex":"#c8c0aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hideaway","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a hiding place, somewhere one can go to get away from other people"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Capable of being stored out of sight when not in use."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hideaway"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hideaway (1937 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Hideaway is a 1937 American comedy film directed by Richard Rosson. Based on the 1937 play A House in the Country by Melvin Levy, the screenplay was written by J. Robert Bren and Edmund L. Hartmann. Produced and distributed by RKO Radio Pictures, it opened on August 13, 1937. The film stars Fred Stone, Emma Dunn, Marjorie Lord and J. Carroll Naish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Hideaway_lobby_card.jpg/330px-Hideaway_lobby_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hideaway_(1937_film)","wikidata":"Q18150657"},{"title":"Hideaway (1995 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Hideaway is a 1995 horror film directed by Brett Leonard. It is based on the 1992 novel of the same name by Dean Koontz, and stars Jeff Goldblum, Christine Lahti, Alicia Silverstone, Jeremy Sisto, Alfred Molina and Rae Dawn Chong."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6e/Hideaway_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hideaway_(1995_film)","wikidata":"Q2364503"},{"title":"Hideaway (Kiesza song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Hideaway\" is the debut single by Canadian recording musician Kiesza from her debut EP of the same name (2014) and her debut studio album, Sound of a Woman (2014). The song was released on April 11, 2014, through Island Records and co-writer Rami Samir Afuni's independent label Lokal Legend as the lead single from both the EP and the album."}],"image":"https://uploa